From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krishna Chaitanya Chundru <krishna.chundru@xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx> (address masked in the archive)
Date: Fri, 2 Jan 2026 04:45:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-x1e80100: Do not turn off PCIe GDSCs during
 gdsc_disable()

With PWRSTS_OFF_ON, PCIe GDSCs are turned off during gdsc_disable(). This
can happen during scenarios such as system suspend and breaks the resume
of PCIe controllers from suspend.

So use PWRSTS_RET_ON to indicate the GDSC driver to not turn off the GDSCs
during gdsc_disable() and allow the hardware to transition the GDSCs to
retention when the parent domain enters low power state during system
suspend.

Fixes: 161b7c401f4b ("clk: qcom: Add Global Clock controller (GCC) driver for X1E80100")
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-x1e80100.c | 16 ++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-x1e80100.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-x1e80100.c
index 8c146d6..fefacae 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-x1e80100.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-x1e80100.c
@@ -6552,7 +6552,7 @@ static struct gdsc gcc_pcie_0_tunnel_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "gcc_pcie_0_tunnel_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
 };
 
@@ -6564,7 +6564,7 @@ static struct gdsc gcc_pcie_1_tunnel_gdsc = {
